From b672694c22ef97d165890c37555b54ba842289ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:55:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(211, veil): a tie stored in master's shape keeps the eyes
 master's DM shut (V4-1)

THE FOURTH REVIEW (REVIEW-VEIL-211-master-client-2026-11-13, lane/review-veil-3-2026-11-12):
every town already saved was saved by master's client. Master's panel addressed a relationship
as relationship.<npc1Id>-<npc2Id>-<type> (db832c892:galleryVeil.js:221); the new rule reads
from/to (141383cd4), and 211 and the client's veil read rows as stored (the client's v1 -> v2
step, which maps npc1Id -> from, runs on load, never on the server). So a description eye or a
whole tie master's DM shut fell away: drawn on the gallery page, and served.

THE CURE: both shapes are the same two ends. Each end reads `from`, else `npc1Id`, else the
name (`to`, `npc2Id`, the name), in CARD_KINDS.relationship.idOf and in 211's
_gallery_veil_card_id; the floor keeps both spellings, as master's kept npc1Id/npc2Id (the
kinds table stays the client's, field for field, galleryServerVeil's pin). A new-shape tie
has no npc1Id and reads as before.

Red at 5a2399cf9, green after (tests/security/galleryVeilCures.pglite.test.js):
- the review row: a town in master's shape, a description eye and a whole tie shut by master's
  addresses, Reveal DM off and on: gallery, link, import, map and page all carried them
  (old dm=false and dm=true, 5 of 5 each) -> none; the same ties in the new shape held before
  and after (the control); the open tie drawn and served (the anchor);
- the client: idOf of a stored tie was relationship.peiyun-huang-jiahao-luo-rival, master's is
  relationship.npc-1-npc-3-rival -> equal, and equal to the migrated twin's; projectShareVeil
  hides them;
- the class: 3,000 fuzzed ties in master's shape: server id = client id = master's id = the
  migrated twin's id (red: 20 of the first 20 shown differ).
Both veil pin files: 42 passed, the one red being V4-2's pin, which is not in this commit.
typecheck:domain:strict 0, typecheck:ratchet 0, eslint 0.

